    "summary": "High‑energy ’72 show with smoking Truckin' > Other One jam",
    "blurb": "Features a scorching Truckin' > The Other One sequence highlighted by Phil’s bass solo, plus strong renditions of Friend Of The Devil and Black Peter. Jerry’s white Strat tone shines throughout, and the band stays locked in despite a brief lyric slip on Bertha.",
    "review": "The August 25, 1972 performance at Berkeley Community Theater captures the Dead in prime form. From the opening Cold Rain And Snow through a tight set that rolls into an explosive Truckin' > The Other One marathon, the band delivers high‑energy playing and flawless interplay. Jerry’s crystal‑clear Strat work is front‑and‑center, especially on the soaring finish to Bertha where he turns a lyrical stumble into a memorable fill. Phil Lesh anchors the jams with a blazing bass solo that lifts Truckin' into uncharted territory, while Bob Weir’s rhythm guitar adds a bright counterpoint on Friend Of The Devil and Black Peter. Keith’s keyboards weave subtle textures beneath the groove, and the dual‑drummer foundation keeps everything grounded. The second set closes with a gorgeous Stella Blue before an exuberant Sugar Magnolia encore, making this night a standout entry in the Spring ’72 tour.",
